## Golang syntax (to be used by AI for notes creation)

1. Initiate a go module using `go mod init [module-name]` 
2. HTTP structure in go: HTTP Request -> Router -> Middleware -> handler() -> Service (internal/external) -> Repository -> PGSQL
3. Different types of types :) int, string, float64, bool and they are 
declared in the most unique way: var fuckityfuck string (var fuckityfuck: string *TS*)
4. Usually don't use precision based integers because it isn't as efficient as go 
adjusting to the platform architecture.
5. Types: We always get 0 values with var (helpful since we can't give undefined to an integer's initialization like in JS) 
6. Empty string: 2 words with first word being a pointer (nil) & second word being empty (value).
7. Struct typing: Parallels from typescript again but not necessarily the same
since Typescript has duck typing